Naming: Standards

Purpose:
  Defines naming conventions for .sdd entities and files.

EntityIDs:
  TASK:
    Format: TASK-NNN or domain prefix (<DOMAIN>-NNN)
    Example: TASK-<ID>, <DOMAIN>-<ID>
  DECISION:
    Format: DEC-NNN
    Example: DEC-<ID>
  SKILL:
    Format: SKILL-NAME
    Example: SKILL-<NAME>
  GATE:
    Format: GATE-TYPE-NNN
    Example: GATE-<TYPE>-<ID>
  WORKFLOW:
    Format: WF-NNN
    Example: WF-021
  MODULE:
    Format: MOD-NAME
    Example: MOD-PAY
  INCIDENT:
    Format: INC-YYYYMMDD-NNN
    Example: INC-091
  RELEASE:
    Format: REL-YYYY-NNN
    Example: REL-2026-08

FileNaming:
  Entity files:
    <id>.sdd
    Example: TASK-1023.sdd, DEC-042.sdd

  INDEX files:
    INDEX.sdd

  Human docs:
    <name>.md
    Example: idempotency.md, payment-flow.md

PrefixSystem:
  @ — entity declaration
  > — comment
  : — property
  = — value
  ? — optional
  ! — required
  ~ — deprecated

RelationshipSyntax:
  depends <id>
  uses <skill>
  blocks <id>
  related <id>
  implements <id>
  supersedes <id>
  conflicts <id>

NamingRules:
  [NM1]  IDs are immutable once assigned.
  [NM2]  File names match entity IDs.
  [NM3]  Prefix system is standard across all .sdd files.
  [NM4]  Relationship syntax uses standard verbs.

State: +
  